msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1189
msgid "Export one page or template area as a deterministic canonical Bricks file plus a compact dependency manifest. Code-sensitive pages fail closed when the caller lacks execute-code permission; checkout never returns a redacted full-replacement candidate. The returned working copy is not authoritative until it passes preview and token-only apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1206
msgid "Preview page workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1207
msgid "Validate, normalize, permission-check, render, diff, and freeze an edited canonical page workspace without saving. Code-sensitive candidates fail closed without execute-code permission. Rejects stale page or design-system baselines."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1224
msgid "Apply page workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1225
msgid "Commit the exact canonical page candidate frozen by preview. Apply accepts no mutable page data, rechecks code-sensitive permissions, and fails closed if authority was lost. Uses the same lock, journal, revision, readback, idempotency, and recovery contract as transactional HTML/CSS import."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1245
msgid "Checkout design resource workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1246
msgid "Export one existing global class, global variable, theme style, or component as a deterministic canonical file with exact resource-specific ownership. This update-only workflow deliberately excludes create, delete, rename, and multi-resource atomicity."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1263
msgid "Preview design resource workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1264
msgid "Side-effect-free validation and diff for one edited design-resource file. Rejects stale item and dependency ownership, immutable IDs, unsupported opaque edits, and unacknowledged component slot removal, then freezes the exact focused mutation in a short-lived user-bound token."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1281
msgid "Apply design resource workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1282
msgid "Commit the exact single-resource mutation frozen by preview. Token-only apply rechecks user, execution policy, write permission, exact resource/dependency baseline, and then delegates normalization, referential validation, compare-and-swap, and readback to the existing focused design ability."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1302
msgid "Commit exact site edits"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1303
msgid "Fastest existing-site path for precise edits: replace page or component text, insert an unstyled native page text sibling, update safe component labels and custom attributes, change global-variable values, or update one global-class/theme-style settings leaf in one call. Pages, components, and design resources may be selected by exact ID or exact unique name; elements may be selected by ID or exact unique current text or label. Each operation must provide expectedValue, or literal allowBlindWrite true only for an intentional target. The server performs canonical resolution, checkout, component-property boundary checks, permissions, CAS preview, durable replay, apply, and authoritative readback internally."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1323
msgid "Checkout site edit map"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1324
msgid "Checkout up to 25 explicit targets through the targets array, using {scope: page, postId} or {scope: design, resource, id}. When IDs are known, filter element outlines with elementIds. Canonical files remain server-side; short selectionRef values bind each typed edit to an authenticated exact selection."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1341
msgid "Preview site edit plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1342
msgid "Compile up to 64 exact typed text or global-variable edits into the frozen canonical files, recheck caller policy and focused write permissions, and delegate validation, stale-state checks, preparation, and preview-token issuance to Site Changeset. No Bricks data is changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1359
msgid "Commit site edit plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1360
msgid "Common two-call existing-site fast path: submit the short selectionRef advertised by checkout with a supported operation and value. Canonical files are compiled and previewed server-side, then Site Changeset applies or resumes under one stable idempotency key. Repeat the same call to recover a lost response; summary readback is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1380
msgid "Checkout site changeset"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1381
msgid "Checkout up to 25 canonical page and design-resource files in one bounded response. Pages are ordered before design resources, so every intermediate pages-first state must be valid. This is a working copy, never an atomic database transaction."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1398
msgid "Preview site changeset"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1399
msgid "Focused-preview every edited file without changing Bricks page or design data, then freeze the exact pages-first changeset in a short-lived user and execution-policy-bound token. Create required design definitions separately before consumers."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: Changeset action, either Apply or Resume.
#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1421
msgid "%s site changeset"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1422
msgid "Run a bounded time slice of the durable changeset. Every inner token and derived key is checkpointed before mutation; just-in-time checkout/rebase preserves target and dependency CAS. Results explicitly report committed, in-progress, partial-commit, failed-before-commit, or manual-recovery state and never claim cross-resource atomicity."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1443
msgid "Commit agent file"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1444
msgid "Validate, durably checkpoint, apply, and authoritatively read back one resolved Bricks file in the second call of a focused edit. Returns a compact digest/version/change summary by default; pass responseFormat=document only when the complete canonical file is needed. The idempotency key is bound to the complete candidate before preview or mutation; retries resume the existing Site Changeset journal and never create a hidden replacement preview."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1464
msgid "Resolve site changeset recovery"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1465
msgid "Delete one terminal durable changeset journal only after an operator has inspected and resolved its partial or manual-recovery state. Requires the exact idempotency key, changeset digest, and literal acknowledgement. This removes recovery evidence but does not roll back or change Bricks data."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1482
msgid "Apply HTML/CSS page import"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1483
msgid "Commit the exact candidate frozen by preview without resending its HTML, CSS, or Bricks tree. Uses database-session fencing, a durable idempotency journal, conditional writes, readback verification, and safe before-image compensation."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1510
msgid "List templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1511
msgid "List all Bricks templates with type, status, and condition summary. Supports pagination and type filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1528
msgid "Get template"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1529
msgid "Fetch a single Bricks template by ID. Returns title, type, status, edit URL, and by default settings plus the element tree for the rendered template area. Pass includeElements=false or includeSettings=false for a lighter response; use get-page-elements when you need scoped element-tree reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1547
msgid "Create a new Bricks template (`bricks_template` post type). Pass `type` (header / footer / content / section / popup / archive / search / error / password_protection, or a WooCommerce type such as wc_product), optional initial `elements` tree, and optional `status` (`draft`, `publish`, or `private`; default `draft`). Returns `templateId`, `editUrl`, and `status`. Note: header and footer templates are automatically wrapped in `<header>` / `<footer>` landmarks at render time. Do NOT set `tag: \"header\"` (or `customTag: \"header\"`) on the template root, because that produces nested landmarks. Use `section` / `block` / `container` with their default tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1563
msgid "Delete template"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1564
msgid "Permanently delete a Bricks template. Destructive and unrecoverable: this calls `wp_delete_post` with `force=true` and there is no Bricks revision path to undo. The response includes a `beforeDelete` snapshot (title, type, element count) so you can show what was removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1581
msgid "Get template settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1582
msgid "Template settings including conditions, header sticky/popup config, password protection, preview."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1599
msgid "Set template settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1600
msgid "Set template settings via partial merge. Covers conditions, header sticky/popup config, password protection."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1617
msgid "Set template conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1618
msgid "Replace the `templateConditions` array on a template. Each condition has a `main` kind (`any`, `frontpage`, `postType`, `archiveType`, `search`, `error`, `terms`, or `ids`) plus kind-specific fields. Section templates can also include `hookName` and optional `hookPriority` to render on a WordPress hook. Legacy `main=hook` input is normalized to `any` when `hookName` is present. Full replacement, not a merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1635
msgid "List template sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1636
msgid "List remote template-library sources: Bricks built-ins (`wireframes`, `design-sets`), admin-configured remote template URLs, and group rows. Returns the raw source records used by the builder source picker. Use a returned `id` or `url` with `bricks/list-remote-templates` to inspect remote templates or `bricks/insert-remote-template` to insert one."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1653
msgid "List remote templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1654
msgid "List templates available in a built-in source (`wireframes` or `design-sets`) or an admin-configured remote template URL. Use a source `id` or `url` from `bricks/list-template-sources`. Returns paginated template metadata by default; request a specific page/perPage and use `mode: \"full\"` only for targeted inspection."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1672
msgid "Copy a local Bricks template's element tree into a target post at a chosen position. Supported positions: `replace` (overwrite everything), `start` and `end` (root-level top or bottom; defaults to `end`), `before` and `after` (sibling of `anchorElementId`), and `append` and `prepend` (child of `anchorElementId`). Every source element ID is regenerated to avoid collisions. A revision is captured before the write, so `replace` is destructive but reversible via `bricks/restore-revision`. For remote library templates use `bricks/insert-remote-template`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1688
msgid "Insert remote template"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1689
msgid "Fetch a template from a remote template-library source such as `wireframes` or `design-sets`, optionally import missing design assets, and insert its element tree into a target post. Uses the same placement options as `bricks/insert-template`. Existing local design assets are preserved and the target post receives a pre-save revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1712
msgid "Get design context"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1713
msgid "One-call summary of the site design context: color palettes, global classes, theme styles, components, global variables, and responsive breakpoints. Pass `responseFormat: \"summary\"` for capped orientation output, or `includeUsage: true` to add `usedOnPosts` per component."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1731
msgid "List color palettes"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1732
msgid "All palettes with complete color records, paletteDigest/colorDigest values, and compact resource ownership. Pass the returned ownership into creates, or add the target digest as itemDigest for updates and deletes."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1749
msgid "Create color"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1750
msgid "Append a builder-shaped color to an existing palette using exact resource ownership from list-color-palettes. Root colors require `light`; shade rows require `parent` and `type`. Returns verified ownership and authoritative color/palette digests."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1766
msgid "Update color"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1767
msgid "Partial-merge update of one palette color using ownership plus its colorDigest as itemDigest. Returns verified ownership and digests. Raw variable renames that would require a cross-resource reference rewrite fail closed without changing palette or reference data."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1784
msgid "Create color palette"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1785
msgid "Create a uniquely named color palette using exact resource ownership from list-color-palettes. Optional builder-shaped colors preserve supplied IDs and shade relationships. Returns verified ownership and authoritative digests."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1801
msgid "Update color palette"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1802
msgid "Rename a color palette using ownership plus its paletteDigest as itemDigest. Does not modify its colors and preserves opaque palette fields. Returns verified ownership and digest."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1819
msgid "Delete color"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1820
msgid "Remove one color using ownership plus its colorDigest as itemDigest. Deleting a root also removes its shades. Removing any named CSS variables requires literal allowOrphans=true even when fresh bounded reference evidence is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1837
msgid "Delete color palette"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1838
msgid "Permanently delete a palette and all its colors using ownership plus its paletteDigest as itemDigest. Removing any named CSS variables requires literal allowOrphans=true even when fresh bounded reference evidence is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1856
msgid "List global classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1857
msgid "All global classes with complete settings, per-class itemDigest, resource ownership, lock ownership, and category ownership. Pass the relevant returned ownership envelopes unchanged when mutating a class."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1874
msgid "Create global class"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1875
msgid "Create a new global class with CSS settings and optional responsive overrides. A non-empty category requires categoryOwnership from list-global-classes and is guarded in the final class commit; split-authority categorized writes fail closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1891
msgid "Batch create global classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1892
msgid "Validate and create many global classes in one atomic write. Requires exact class ownership and, when any class is categorized, categoryOwnership from the same latest read. Category existence and authority are guarded. Prefer this for converter output; provided 6-character IDs are preserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1908
msgid "Update global class"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1909
msgid "Update an existing global class without losing opaque stored fields. Requires class ownership with the full-row itemDigest plus lock ownership; assigning a non-empty category also requires categoryOwnership from the same read. Exact lock and category rows are guarded in the final commit. Settings merge and selectors replace."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1926
msgid "Delete global class"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1927
msgid "Permanently delete a global class. Requires class ownership, lock ownership, and literal allowOrphans=true even when fresh bounded usage evidence is zero. Shared-authority deletes fail closed when the local scan is incomplete."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1945
msgid "Get theme styles"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1946
msgid "Theme styles with exact resource ownership and per-style digests calculated from complete authoritative rows. Without a filter returns summaries; with a style ID returns its full unredacted settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1963
msgid "List theme styles"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1964
msgid "Paginated theme-style summaries with exact resource ownership and full-row itemDigest. Use get-theme-styles with an id for the complete settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1981
msgid "Create theme style"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1982
msgid "Create a new theme style through a fresh exact append compare-and-swap. Returns refreshed ownership and a digest of the complete stored style. Pass `conditions: [{ main: \"any\" }]` for site-wide defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1998
msgid "Update theme style"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:1999
msgid "Update an existing theme style with exact ownership and its full-row itemDigest. Opaque stored fields are preserved. Settings merge by default; `replace: true` replaces settings, while label and conditions replace when provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2016
msgid "Delete theme style"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2017
msgid "Delete a theme style with exact ownership and its full-row itemDigest. Styles with settings or conditions require literal acknowledgeStyleRemoval=true after reviewing fresh bounded impact evidence. Returns the complete unredacted deleted row for manual recovery."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2035
msgid "List components"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2036
msgid "List all components with labels, property summaries, componentDigest values, and the atomically paired designSystemVersion. Use the digest and version together for safe update/delete calls. Supports pagination."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2053
msgid "Get component"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2054
msgid "Component elements, properties, variants, slots, authoritative componentDigest, and atomically paired designSystemVersion for safe follow-up writes. Reports componentPayloadRedacted when code-sensitive settings are hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2072
msgid "Create a new component from an elements subtree. Labels must be unique (`bricks_conflict_duplicate_component_name` on collision). Incoming element ids are regenerated, property connections and parent-property references are remapped, and builder metadata is stamped so the component is not treated as a beta component."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2088
msgid "Update component"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2089
msgid "Update an existing component. Requires expectedDesignSystemVersion and expectedComponentDigest from a recent list/get response. Only provided fields are changed, but `elements` replaces the entire component tree, so read the component first with `bricks/get-component` before editing one element. When componentPayloadRedacted is true, do not replace elements from that redacted payload. Slot IDs are preserved where possible; removing any existing slot requires explicit `allowSlotOrphans=true`, even when the fresh usage scan finds no content."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2106
msgid "Delete component"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2107
msgid "Remove a component from the global store. Requires expectedDesignSystemVersion, expectedComponentDigest, expectedUsageCount from a recent read, and explicit `allowOrphans=true` for every deletion, including zero known uses. The digest covers the complete authoritative component. Usage is current review evidence, not a guarantee that every reference was found."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2124
msgid "Extract component from elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2125
msgid "Lift an existing element subtree out of a post and into a new global component, replacing the original subtree with a component instance. External references inside the subtree (global class names, CSS variables) are preserved as-is, so the component stays coupled to whatever tokens the original elements used. A revision is captured before the post write."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2143
msgid "List global variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2144
msgid "All global CSS variables and categories with authority-correct ownership plus ready full-row itemOwnership envelopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2161
msgid "Set global variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2162
msgid "Ownership-guarded variable upsert. Accepts copy-ready rows from list-global-variables, requires the variable and category ownerships from one latest read, preserves opaque fields, and rejects or compensates category drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2179
msgid "Set global variable categories"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2180
msgid "Replace the complete global-variable category list with exact category and variable ownership from one latest read. Referenced removals and scale-config changes fail closed because no acknowledgement can make the required variable regeneration atomic. Returns refreshed ownership and ready per-category item ownership."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2200
msgid "Delete global variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2201
msgid "Delete one global CSS variable with its ready itemOwnership from the latest read. Requires literal allowOrphans=true even when fresh bounded reference evidence is zero; shared-authority deletes fail closed when the local scan is incomplete. Success verifies the variable remains absent."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2218
msgid "Generate scale variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2219
msgid "Preview fluid clamp() variables with a deterministic generationDigest and exact variable/category save ownership. Direct scale persistence fails closed until the two option stores can be committed atomically; persist reviewed rows through ownership-guarded abilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2235
msgid "Audit design system"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2236
msgid "Read-only scan for design-system rot: orphan references (errors), theme styles without conditions (warnings), unused resources and palette fragmentation (infos). Scans all Bricks posts + templates in one pass. Pass `scope` to narrow, or `skipPostScan: true` for a fast config-only check."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2253
msgid "Generate color shades"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2254
msgid "Generate builder-equivalent light, dark, or transparent shades. A preview targeting an existing palette color returns saveOwnership; pass it unchanged with save:true to replace the matching shade graph through owned CAS. Inline baseColor previews remain persistence-free."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2281, ../includes/elements/form.php:142, ../includes/integrations/form/init.php:1668
msgid "Create post"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2282
msgid "Create a new page or post. Optionally seed a Bricks element tree atomically with creation. Returns the new post ID, builder URL, and revision ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2298
msgid "Duplicate post"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2299
msgid "Clone a post/page including its Bricks element tree, page settings, and featured image. The duplicate is created as a draft by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2315
msgid "Delete post"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2316
msgid "Move a post or page to trash (recoverable) or permanently delete it. Lock-aware: refuses to delete a post that another user is currently editing."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2344
msgid "List revisions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2345
msgid "List Bricks-aware revisions for a post. Shows which areas (content/header/footer) each revision has data for."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2362
msgid "Get revision"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2363
msgid "Fetch the full Bricks element tree from a specific revision. Read-only; use `bricks/restore-revision` to roll back."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2380
msgid "Restore revision"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2381
msgid "Roll back a post to a previous revision. Copies Bricks postmeta (element tree + page settings) from the revision onto the current post. Takes a new snapshot first so the restore itself is reversible."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2410
msgid "Upload a media file from a URL or base64 data. Returns the attachment object with all size variants, ready to use in Bricks image elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2426
msgid "Find media"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2427
msgid "Search the media library by filename, title, or alt text. Filter by MIME type. Supports compact results or full media objects with all size variants."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2444
msgid "Delete media"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2445
msgid "Delete a media library attachment by ID. Use after upload-media QA runs or when replacing unused assets. Destructive: returns a beforeDelete snapshot and respects WordPress attachment trash behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2469
msgid "Get Bricks MCP version"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2470
msgid "Report the Bricks plugin version, the Bricks abilities contract version, the WordPress MCP Adapter version, and the WordPress core version. Call once at the start of a session to detect version drift mid-conversation. `disabledAbilityCount` includes both admin-disabled and default-off abilities; `adminDisabledAbilityCount` and `defaultDisabledAbilityCount` split those states."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2487
msgid "List Bricks ability status"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2488
msgid "Inspect whether expected Bricks abilities are enabled. Pass exact `abilityNames` for targeted diagnostics. The default summary lists enabled abilities only; pass `includeDisabled: true` for the complete compact registry, or use `detailed` for full metadata. Exact-name lookups still return matching disabled abilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2505
msgid "Bricks orientation (start here)"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2506
msgid "Compact task router for clients without loaded Bricks skills. A clearly named existing page or design resource routes directly to resolve-agent-file then commit-agent-file without version, context, catalog, or manifest calls. Pass responseFormat=detailed only when the complete workflow guide is needed. Clients that already loaded bricks-start-here do not need this tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2533
msgid "List CMS sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2534
msgid "Introspect the site's content model. Pass a `source` (one of `wp`, `acf`, `jetengine`, `metabox`, `cmb2`, `pods`, `toolset`, `woo`) to fetch its schema, or omit to receive only the availability directory. Read-only: Bricks does not expose CRUD for third-party field providers. Use this to understand what data the site already carries so you can reference it correctly in templates and dynamic-data tags."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2551
msgid "Get reading settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2552
msgid "Read WordPress Reading settings: whether the front page shows latest posts or a static page, the selected homepage, and the selected posts page."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2569
msgid "Set reading settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2570
msgid "Set WordPress Reading settings for site builds. Covers `show_on_front`, `page_on_front`, and `page_for_posts` only. Requires manage_options."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2594
msgid "List nav menus"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2595
msgid "List WordPress nav menus with item counts, assigned theme locations, and whether any menu item uses Bricks mega-menu or multilevel metadata. Read-only. Use before deciding whether to reuse an existing WordPress menu or build a new Nav Nested menu directly in a Bricks header."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2612
msgid "Get nav menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2613
msgid "Fetch one WordPress nav menu as an ordered nested item tree. Includes menu item links, object references, classes, target/rel fields, assigned locations, and Bricks item options (`megaMenuTemplateId`, `multilevel`). Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2630
msgid "Save nav menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2631
msgid "Create or update a WordPress nav menu, assign registered theme locations, and create/update/reorder menu items from a nested tree. Omitted existing items are preserved, not deleted; use `bricks/delete-nav-menu-items` for explicit item deletion. Supports Bricks item options for top-level items: `megaMenuTemplateId` attaches a published Bricks template for the Nav Menu element mega-menu path, and `multilevel` enables Bricks multilevel behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2648
msgid "Delete nav menu items"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2649
msgid "Delete explicit WordPress nav menu item IDs from a selected menu. Destructive and not Bricks revision-backed; returns beforeDelete snapshots for every removed item. Never use this for reordering or partial updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2669
msgid "Delete nav menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2670
msgid "Delete a WordPress nav menu by ID, slug, or exact name. Destructive and not Bricks revision-backed; returns a full beforeDelete snapshot including menu items and Bricks mega-menu metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2701
msgid "Get form config"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2702
msgid "Read a Form element's fields, actions, and settings for a given post + elementId. Read-only. Use before update-form-fields / update-form-actions to see current shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2719
msgid "Update form fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2720
msgid "Replace the entire `fields` array on a Form element. Order is significant, so this is always a full replacement, never a merge. Each field needs at least `{ id, type }`, and `type` must be one of the 18 supported field types (see `skills/forms`). A pre-save revision is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2737
msgid "Update form actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2738
msgid "Update the actions list and/or partial-merge per-action settings (emailTo, webhookUrl, redirectUrl, etc.). Built-in actions are validated against the same runtime list the Form element uses, so `save-submission` and `unlock-password-protection` require their global settings. Custom action keys are accepted only when a matching `bricks/form/action/{key}` hook is registered. Provide at least one of `actions` or `settings`. A pre-save revision is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2755
msgid "List form submissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2756
msgid "Read stored submissions for a Form element from the `{prefix}bricks_form_submissions` table. Paginated. When the table is missing (the Save Submission action has never run), returns an empty list with an explanatory `note` rather than a hard error."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2784
msgid "List query filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2785
msgid "Enumerate Query Filter elements across posts/templates (filter-checkbox, filter-radio, filter-select, filter-range, filter-search, filter-datepicker, filter-submit, filter-active-filters). Returns post/location + filter target (filterQueryId). Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2802
msgid "Get filter element"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2803
msgid "Read a single Query Filter element's full settings (source, field, label, style, filterQueryId, etc.). Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2820
msgid "Update filter element"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2821
msgid "Partial-merge update of a filter element's settings. Use to change source (taxonomy/customField/wpField), field mapping, labels, or UI options without touching filterQueryId. For retargeting to a different loop, use set-filter-target-query. A pre-save revision is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2838
msgid "Set filter target query"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2839
msgid "Bind a filter element to a target query-loop element via `filterQueryId`. Filter elements that lack this binding never fire. Pass an empty string to unbind. A pre-save revision is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2856
msgid "Reindex filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2857
msgid "Drop/recreate the query-filter index table and queue index jobs. Use after bulk filter changes, schema changes, or to recover from a corrupted index. The background job may continue after this call returns. Equivalent to clicking Regenerate filter index in Bricks > Settings > Query filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2884
msgid "List popups"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2885
msgid "List all popup templates (`bricks_template` posts whose template type is `popup`). Returns id, title, status, and conditions summary. Read-only. Equivalent to list-templates with type=popup plus extra popup-specific meta."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2902
msgid "Get popup config"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2903
msgid "Read a popup template's configuration: the template conditions (where it can appear), the popup-specific settings (`popupCloseOn`, `popupBodyScroll`, `popupAjax`, `popupLimit*`), and the interaction triggers that reference it (elements whose target is `popup` with `templateId` pointing at this popup). Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2920
msgid "Update popup settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2921
msgid "Partial-merge update of popup-specific template settings: popupCloseOn (esc/backdrop), popupBodyScroll, popupAjax, popupLimitWindow, popupLimitSessionStorage, popupLimitLocalStorage, and popupLimitTimeStorage. Does NOT manage template display conditions (use set-template-conditions) or interaction triggers on opener elements (use update-element-interactions on the caller)."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2949
msgid "Get element interactions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2950
msgid "Read an element's own `_interactions` rows plus inherited global-class interactions in frontend order. Each interaction has a trigger (such as `click`, `enterView`, `scroll`, `formSubmit`) and an action (such as `show`, `hide`, `setAttribute`, `startAnimation`, `toggleOffCanvas`, `javascript`, `storageAdd`). `target` is optional and defaults to `self` at runtime; valid explicit values are `self`, `custom`, and `popup`. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2967
msgid "Update element interactions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2968
msgid "Replace the element-level `_interactions` array. Order is significant, so this is always a full replacement, never a merge. Missing row IDs are generated. Trigger, action, target, JavaScript function references, and action/trigger-specific required fields are validated. Global-class interactions are read-only here; update the class to change inherited rows. A pre-save revision is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2996
msgid "Get element conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:2997
msgid "Read the `_conditions` array stored on an element's settings. Conditions are OR groups containing AND items: the element renders when any group matches and every item inside that group matches. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3014
msgid "Update element conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3015
msgid "Replace the `_conditions` array on an element. Conditions are full-replacement ordered repeaters, never a merge. Missing row IDs are generated. Pass an empty array to clear all conditions. A pre-save revision is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3043
msgid "List Bricks settings schema"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3044
msgid "Discover which Bricks global-settings keys are writable via MCP. Returns an allow-list registry: each entry declares `key`, `type`, `category` (general/performance/maintenance/builder/templates/forms), `label`, and validation hints. Call this before `bricks/set-global-settings` to know what you can touch. Credentials, code-execution toggles, and builder role data are excluded from this surface; use list-credential-status to check whether credentials are configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3061
msgid "List Bricks credential status"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3062
msgid "Read whether Bricks credentials are configured without returning secret values. Covers the license key, API/site/secret keys, access tokens, and template passwords. Every row returns configured/readable/writable flags; readable and writable are false because credential values stay admin-UI-only for now."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3079
msgid "Get Bricks global settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3080
msgid "Read current values for every allow-listed Bricks global setting. Excluded keys (credentials and code-execution settings) are never returned even if set. Remote template source passwords are redacted to passwordConfigured booleans. Pair with `bricks/list-settings-schema` to know what each key means."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3097
msgid "Set Bricks global settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3098
msgid "Partial-merge write to Bricks global settings. Pass `{ settings: { key: value, ... } }`; only the keys you send are touched, and everything else is preserved. Keys outside the registry return `bricks_setting_unknown`, and excluded keys return `bricks_setting_excluded`. Every value is validated against the registry schema before write."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3122
msgid "Get WooCommerce setup status"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3123
msgid "Inspect Bricks/WooCommerce setup readiness for shop, single product, cart, checkout, and account areas. Returns assigned pages, existing Bricks data/content risks, available classic/v2 presets, Bricks Woo settings, and WooCommerce core page/account/checkout settings. Read this before planning or running Woo setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3140
msgid "Plan WooCommerce setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3141
msgid "Dry-run Bricks WooCommerce setup. Produces a planId plus page creation/reuse/assignment operations, selected classic or advanced presets, template-drafting side effects, blockers, warnings, and confirmation requirements. Defaults to classic mode because modular v2 Woo elements are experimental."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3158
msgid "Run WooCommerce setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3159
msgid "Apply a reviewed Woo setup plan: create only missing Woo pages, reuse matching pages only when empty or shortcode-only, assign Woo page options, optionally enable experimental advanced modular elements, and run the shared Woo setup wizard for selected areas. Existing Bricks/non-empty/block page content requires explicit overwriteExistingPageContent and destructive confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3176
msgid "Get Woo setup options"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3177
msgid "Read the safe WooCommerce core options that Bricks setup needs: assigned shop/cart/checkout/account pages, coupon/login/registration checkout settings, and native archive AJAX add-to-cart behavior. Bricks-owned Woo toggles remain in bricks/get-global-settings. Credentials and payment/shipping gateway settings are not exposed."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3194
msgid "Set Woo setup options"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3195
msgid "Partial-merge write to the small allow-list of WooCommerce core options Bricks setup needs. Page IDs must reference existing non-trashed pages or 0 to clear, boolean values are stored as WooCommerce yes/no options, and unrelated Woo settings are preserved. Bricks-owned Woo toggles remain in bricks/set-global-settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3219
msgid "List Bricks builder permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3220
msgid "Read the real builder-access model: permission sections, default and custom capability definitions, and the current WordPress role assignments. Custom definitions live in `BRICKS_DB_CAPABILITIES_PERMISSIONS`; role access lives on WordPress roles, not in `bricks_global_settings`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3237
msgid "Upsert Bricks builder capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3238
msgid "Create or update one custom builder access capability. The capability grants a validated list of builder permission keys and then appears in the Builder access role selector. Built-in Bricks capability ids cannot be overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3255
msgid "Set Bricks builder role access"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3256
msgid "Assign existing builder access capabilities to WordPress roles. Empty string means no builder access. The administrator role is intentionally not writable here because Bricks always treats administrators as full access."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3273
msgid "Delete Bricks builder capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3274
msgid "Delete one custom builder capability definition and remove that WordPress capability from all roles. Built-in Bricks capabilities cannot be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3305
msgid "List Bricks breakpoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3306
msgid "Read the site's responsive breakpoints. Returns `{ baseKey, baseWidth, customEnabled, isMobileFirst, breakpoints, defaults }`, with `breakpoints` sorted by width for the active paradigm. `customEnabled` reflects the `customBreakpoints` master toggle."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3323
msgid "Set Bricks breakpoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3324
msgid "Full-replacement write of the breakpoint list with exact ownership. Removing or renaming any current key requires literal allowRemovedBreakpoints=true and returns removed keys plus bounded usage evidence; width, label, icon, ordering, and additive edits do not require acknowledgement. Exactly one row must have base: true. When cssLoading=file, follow up with bricks/regenerate-css-files."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3355
msgid "List global queries"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3356
msgid "Enumerate the reusable query-loop configurations saved in Bricks. Supports search, category filter, and pagination. Returns a summary row per query (`id`, `label`, `category`, and a `summary` object with fields such as `objectType`, `postType`, and `posts_per_page`) plus the category list. Call `bricks/get-global-query` to fetch the full stored row."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3373
msgid "Get global query"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3374
msgid "Read a single global query by ID. Returns the full stored row, including `id`, `name`, optional `category`, and `settings` using the same shape as an element's inline `query` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3391
msgid "Create global query"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3392
msgid "Save a new reusable query. Use a unique label and a `query` object that mirrors an element's inline `query` setting (for example `{ objectType: \"post\", postType: [\"post\"], posts_per_page: 10 }`). Any optional `category` must already exist; create it first via `bricks/create-global-query-category`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3408
msgid "Update global query"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3409
msgid "Partial-merge update of a global query's label, category, or inline query object. When the `query` field is sent it is replaced in full (no deep merge inside), so always pass the complete query-settings object."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3426
msgid "Delete global query"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3427
msgid "Delete a global query by ID. Elements referencing the deleted query will fall back to their inline query settings (if any) or show no loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3447
msgid "Create global query category"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3448
msgid "Create a new category that global queries can be grouped under. Returns the generated `{ id, name }` category row."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3464
msgid "Delete global query category"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3465
msgid "Delete a global-query category. Queries inside the category are kept; their `category` field is cleared."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3496
msgid "List Bricks sidebars"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3497
msgid "Enumerate custom sidebars registered via Bricks > Settings > Sidebars. Read-only. Returns `[{ id, name, description }]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3514
msgid "Create Bricks sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3515
msgid "Register a new custom sidebar. The ID is derived from `name` (lowercased, spaces to underscores, stripped of other characters). Names must be unique. Once created, the sidebar shows up in the Bricks \"Sidebar\" element dropdown and accepts widgets via Appearance > Widgets."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3531
msgid "Update Bricks sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3532
msgid "Partial-merge update of a sidebar's `name` and/or `description`. The `id` is immutable; to change it, delete and recreate the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3549
msgid "Delete Bricks sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3550
msgid "Delete a custom sidebar by ID. Widgets placed in the sidebar are removed from `sidebars_widgets` (same behavior as the admin UI). Destructive."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3581
msgid "List Bricks custom fonts"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3582
msgid "Enumerate custom font families registered via the `bricks_fonts` CPT. Returns paginated rows with `id`, `family`, and `faceCount`; call `bricks/get-custom-font` for the full `fontFaces` map."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3599
msgid "Get Bricks custom font"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3600
msgid "Fetch a single custom font family by post ID. Returns `{ font: { id, family, fontFaces } }`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3617
msgid "Create Bricks custom font family"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3618
msgid "Create a `bricks_fonts` family from `family`. Returns `{ font: { id, family, fontFaces } }`. Attach face files via `bricks/upload-custom-font-file` and `bricks/update-custom-font`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3634
msgid "Update Bricks custom font"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3635
msgid "Update a custom font family. Accepts `family` for renaming and `fontFaces` for full replacement of the face map, keyed by weight/style strings such as `400` or `400italic`. Every file value must reference an attachment ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3652
msgid "Delete Bricks custom font"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3653
msgid "Delete a custom font family post. Face attachments stay in the media library; remove them separately if they are no longer needed. Destructive: pages using the font will fall back to their next available choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3673
msgid "Upload Bricks custom font file"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3674
msgid "Upload a font face file (woff2, woff, ttf, otf, or eot) as a private attachment. Enforces an extension allow-list, MIME sniffing via `wp_check_filetype_and_ext`, and an 8 MB size cap (filterable via `bricks/abilities/fonts/max_bytes`). Returns the new attachment ID; pass it to `bricks/update-custom-font` to bind it to a weight and style."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3697
msgid "List Bricks icon sets"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3698
msgid "Enumerate custom icon sets (`BRICKS_DB_ICON_SETS`) and the list of disabled built-in or custom icon-set IDs (`BRICKS_DB_DISABLED_ICON_SETS`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3715
msgid "Set disabled Bricks icon sets"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3716
msgid "Full-replacement write of the disabled-icon-set list. Use this to hide built-in libraries or custom icon sets from the builder picker. Pass an empty array to re-enable all."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3733
msgid "List Bricks custom icons"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3734
msgid "Enumerate uploaded custom SVG icon rows from `BRICKS_DB_CUSTOM_ICONS`, optionally filtered by `setId`. Rows use the builder icon-manager shape: `id`, `setId`, `name`, `url`, and `attachment_id`. Paginated."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3751
msgid "Upload Bricks custom icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3752
msgid "Add an SVG icon to an existing custom icon set. The raw SVG is sanitized server-side, stored as a Media Library attachment, then saved in `BRICKS_DB_CUSTOM_ICONS` with `url` and `attachment_id` so the builder icon manager can use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3768
msgid "Delete Bricks custom icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3769
msgid "Remove a custom icon by ID from the `BRICKS_DB_CUSTOM_ICONS` option. Destructive."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3789
msgid "Create Bricks custom icon set"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3790
msgid "Create a new custom icon set so `upload-custom-icon` has a `setId` target. Appends a row to `BRICKS_DB_ICON_SETS` with a generated `set_<hex>` ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3806
msgid "Delete Bricks custom icon set"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3807
msgid "Remove a custom icon set from `BRICKS_DB_ICON_SETS`. Cascades to drop every custom icon row in `BRICKS_DB_CUSTOM_ICONS` assigned to that set. SVG attachments stay in the Media Library. Destructive."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3834
msgid "List Bricks pseudo-classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3835
msgid "Return the list of pseudo-class selectors available in the builder style panel. `isDefault` is true when the option is unset and Bricks is using the built-in fallback (`:hover`, `:active`, `:focus`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3852
msgid "Set Bricks pseudo-classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3853
msgid "Full-replacement write of the pseudo-class selector list with exact ownership. Removing any current selector requires literal allowRemovedPseudoClasses=true and returns removed selectors plus bounded usage evidence; additive and reorder-only edits do not require acknowledgement. Empty/null resets to the built-in defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3880
msgid "Get Bricks style manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3881
msgid "Return the `BRICKS_DB_STYLE_MANAGER` option verbatim, or null if unset. Common keys: `htmlFontSize`, `minScreenWidth`, `maxScreenWidth`, `defaultMode` (light|dark|auto)."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3898
msgid "Set Bricks style manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3899
msgid "Full-replacement write of the style-manager option. Pass null or empty object to reset to defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3926
msgid "Regenerate Bricks CSS files"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3927
msgid "Mirror of Settings > Bricks > General > \"Regenerate CSS files\". Rebuilds the per-post CSS files served when `cssLoading` is `file`. When `cssLoading` is `inline`, the regenerated files act only as a fallback; the live output is still inline `<style>` tags."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3944
msgid "List orphaned Bricks elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3945
msgid "Scan every post that uses Bricks meta for elements whose parent no longer exists in the same tree. Read-only: returns what `bricks/cleanup-orphaned-elements` would remove without touching anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3962
msgid "Clean up orphaned Bricks elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3963
msgid "Strip orphan rows from the Bricks postmeta of every affected post. Destructive. Mirrors the admin \"Clean up orphaned elements\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3995
msgid "Execute PHP"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:3996
msgid "Run arbitrary PHP for advanced development, maintenance, automation, and troubleshooting workflows. Requires explicit PHP configuration and Bricks code execution access for the connected user."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4023
msgid "List Bricks transfer items"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4024
msgid "Read the unified import/export selector for the current site. Returns exportable transfer types and exact item IDs for color palettes, theme styles, classes, variables, custom fonts, breakpoints, global queries, components, templates, settings tabs, builder interface profiles, and custom capabilities, filtered by the current user permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4041
msgid "Export Bricks transfer package"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4042
msgid "Create a unified Bricks import/export ZIP package and return it as base64 for MCP transport. Call `bricks/list-transfer-items` first and pass explicit item IDs for every selected type. Sensitive settings tabs (`api-keys`, `custom-code`) require `allowSensitiveSettings: true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4059
msgid "Inspect Bricks transfer package"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4060
msgid "Inspect a base64 unified transfer ZIP without writing. Returns the manifest filtered by current user permissions plus conflicts, warnings, `zipHash`, and size. Call this before `bricks/import-transfer-package` and pass the returned `zipHash` as `expectedZipHash`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4077
msgid "Import Bricks transfer package"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4078
msgid "Import selected items from an inspected unified transfer ZIP. Requires explicit `types`, exact manifest item IDs, and `expectedZipHash` from `bricks/inspect-transfer-package`. Defaults to keeping existing data on conflicts. Any replacement requires `allowOverwrite: true`; sensitive settings tabs require `allowSensitiveSettings: true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4102
msgid "Get Bricks system information"
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4103
msgid "Read-only environment snapshot covering theme, Bricks, WordPress, server, and active plugins. Mirrors Settings > Bricks > System Information. License and API key values are never included."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/manager.php:4509
msgid "Page number (1-indexed). Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:56
msgid "Version of the active Bricks plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:60
msgid "Version of the Bricks abilities contract. Bumps on breaking changes to ability signatures, error codes, or response shapes."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:64
msgid "Version of the WordPress mcp-adapter plugin, or null if not detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:68
msgid "WordPress core version."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:72
msgid "Whether wp_register_ability is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:76
msgid "Total number of currently disabled abilities, including admin-disabled abilities and default-off categories. Call `bricks-list-ability-status` to see which."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:80
msgid "Number of abilities explicitly disabled by the admin under Bricks > Settings > AI."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:84
msgid "Number of abilities disabled because their category is default-off and has not been explicitly enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:145
msgid "Optional exact ability names to inspect, such as `bricks/update-element`. Exact-name diagnostics return matching disabled abilities without requiring includeDisabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:152
msgid "Include disabled rows in an unfiltered summary. Omit for the compact enabled-ability inventory. Detailed responses continue to include the complete registry."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:158
msgid "Summary returns compact status rows and, by default, only enabled abilities. Detailed includes labels, descriptions, annotations, and the complete registry."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:177
msgid "Requested Bricks ability status rows. An unfiltered summary returns enabled abilities by default; pass includeDisabled to include the complete registry."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:289
msgid "Compact returns only task routing. Detailed returns the complete bundled workflow guide."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:309
msgid "Response detail level used for orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:313
msgid "Markdown-formatted task routing or complete orientation prose."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:317
msgid "Hyphenated MCP tool names exposed directly on this site (visible in `tools/list`). Example: ability `bricks/get-design-context` appears as tool `bricks-get-design-context`. The list reflects the current admin deny-list and any `bricks/abilities/named_tools` filter overrides."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/meta.php:322
msgid "Call shape for invoking long-tail abilities (those not in `fastPath`) through the bundled mcp-adapter dispatcher tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/navigation.php:85
msgid "Menu name. Required when creating a new menu. When menuId/slug is provided, renames the existing menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/navigation.php:89
msgid "Optional menu description. Pass an empty string to clear."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/navigation.php:93
msgid "Theme location slugs to assign this menu to. Omitted locations are preserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/navigation.php:98
msgid "Theme location slugs to clear."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/navigation.php:103
msgid "Ordered nested menu item tree to create/update/reorder. Omitted existing items are preserved, not deleted. Use delete-nav-menu-items for explicit deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/navigation.php:142
msgid "Nav menu term ID containing the items."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/abilities/navigation.php:146
msgid "Explicit nav menu item post IDs to delete."
